<p>The U.S. military said it struck a boat in the eastern Pacific Ocean on Sunday, killing three people it accused of taking part in narcotics trafficking operations. U.S. Southern Command said intelligence showed the vessel moving along known trafficking routes, and The Hindu reported that the military described it as linked to designated terrorist organizations. Video released by the military showed a fast-moving boat before an explosion left it burning. The strike is the latest in a string of U.S. attacks on suspected drug boats since September, part of an intensified campaign under President Trump that has now killed at least 185 people, according to an Agence France-Presse tally cited by several outlets. The operation underscores the administration’s increasingly forceful maritime counter-narcotics strategy in the eastern Pacific.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/iuv_Rhu64uFN5wV1tu56kRpkPdtzV_QxL2k4nj4Fw7fGBqAFSStihvkwQbuzaM2YJDEzW9BvmPEZS9j8OvVIuDsr8FC2SC9wxCE8prHkJ6HvZQrlxHAiaShaSwPWxX8CGJPjE_6nNqsJfxzjrtXA8WOci8yTBK7XJ2bB6DYaBiWh3mvxuZOai_zsNe4m88oEaCk' alt='An image from a video provided by the U.S. military shows what it said was a strike on a boat in the eastern Pacific Ocean on Sunday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Dozens of strikes: The New York Times said the United States has carried out dozens of boat strikes in the region since September against people the administration accuses of drug smuggling.</li><li>Video evidence: The Guardian reported that military footage showed the vessel speeding across open water moments before the blast and fire.</li><li>Known corridor: U.S. officials said the boat was traveling in the eastern Pacific along routes authorities identify as established narco-trafficking corridors.</li><li>Rising toll: Agence France-Presse’s tally, cited by multiple outlets, puts the death toll from this U.S. campaign at at least 185 people.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Southern Command: The military said the vessel was engaged in narco-trafficking operations and that intelligence placed it on known trafficking routes in the eastern Pacific. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/usa-military-strikes-on-drug-boat-in-pacific-ocean-death-toll/article70910847.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Trump administration: The administration has framed the maritime campaign as part of a broader effort to target people it accuses of smuggling drugs by sea, with strikes continuing for several months. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/27/world/americas/us-military-boat-strike-pacific-drugs.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Agence France-Presse tally cited by outlets: The cumulative death count cited across reports shows how lethal the campaign has become as repeated strikes continue in the same maritime theater. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-says-three-killed-in-boat-strike-as-campaign-toll-hits-185'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/apr/27/us-three-killed-boat-alleged-narco-eastern-pacific'>US strike kills three on alleged narco boat as campaign death toll hits 185</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/boat-strike-eastern-pacific-kills-3/'>Another strike on alleged drug boat kills 3 in eastern Pacific, military says</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/27/world/americas/us-military-boat-strike-pacific-drugs.html'>U.S. Military Strikes Another Boat in Eastern Pacific, Killing 3</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/usa-military-strikes-on-drug-boat-in-pacific-ocean-death-toll/article70910847.ece'>U.S. says three killed in boat strike as campaign toll hits 185</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-says-three-killed-in-boat-strike-as-campaign-toll-hits-185'>US says three killed in boat strike as campaign toll hits 185<